(geometry-meridional-chord)=
### Axial meridional chord

`geometry.meridional_chord` · GUI section 01 · axial reference

Axial separation of camberline endpoints.

**Illustrative range:** 90%, 95%, 100% and 110% of the reference chord, at fixed count and radius.

**Admissible inputs:** > 0 mm; coupled geometry checks also apply. These are mathematical bounds, not aerodynamic design limits or slider endpoints.

**Visible effect:** Scales both camber and nominal thickness in physical units; rounded edges can protrude beyond the endpoints.

**Coupling and limitations:** All thickness ratios remain fixed, so dimensional thickness changes naturally. Pitch stays fixed and large chords can collide with neighbors. Inactive for radial geometry.

| Reference | Sweep values (baseline in bold) | Rejected values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reaction | 13.5 mm, 14.25 mm, **15 mm**, 16.5 mm | None |
| Impulse | 48.6 mm, 51.3 mm, **54 mm**, 59.4 mm | None |

**Reaction** — camberline, half paired thickness, blade profiles.

