### Leading shoulder fullness

`thickness.leading_edge_fullness` · GUI section 03 · axial reference

Independent rational modification of the leading reference shoulder.

**Illustrative range:** Baseline offsets -0.1, -0.05, 0 and +0.1 explore local shoulder changes inside the individual bounds.

**Admissible inputs:** >= -0.5; <= 0.5; coupled geometry checks also apply. These are mathematical bounds, not aerodynamic design limits or slider endpoints.

**Visible effect:** Negative values narrow and positive values fill the shoulder; zero at both ends recovers the Denton body.

**Coupling and limitations:** The modification has global support. The trailing fullness is fixed, and some opposed pairs fail the joint rational-denominator check.

| Reference | Sweep values (baseline in bold) | Rejected values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reaction | -0.1, -0.05, **0**, 0.1 | None |
| Impulse | -0.35, -0.3, **-0.25**, -0.15 | None |

