## Generated validation record

The recorded run contains **212 requested cases: 212 accepted, 0 rejected**, sweeping 28 GUI fields while holding blade count fixed. Each continuous parameter has four values including the baseline; categorical and Boolean parameters use their available choices. Every image has one row and three columns, thin lines, a full box on each panel, and plasma colors sampled from 0.25 to 0.75. All accepted cases passed independent-input isolation, baseline recovery when applicable, mapped-thickness consistency, and sampled self/neighbor intersection checks. Rejected cases, if any, are reported beside their figures and never drawn as accepted geometry.

The manifest contains every resolved input, warning, diagnostic, source hash, coordinate hash, figure hash and physical-aspect check. Intersection checks apply at the requested resolution; they are not proofs between samples. A nonpositive normal-map margin is reported as a caution by the kernel even if the sampled contour passes intersection checks.
